Z||000007||87GTZ34||05-11-2001||05:36 PM||||FT - You may want to try to uplug lights by groups.  ie. the tail lights try it, side markers try it, front try it, dash try it.  Of course, I would try to unplug as much of the wiring harness connectors as possible in order to isolate it faster.  If you need for me to look up in the factory manual where the respective connectors are, I will help.<P>GL||||reg||3
Z||000008||FieroTig||05-12-2001||01:48 AM||||thanks guys.. i figured it out. but i had no clue what it was.. it turns out i had a bad dimmer switch, found one at the local salvage yard. car works great. thanks for all help. i am working on selling the car, it's a 85 gt red/grey ground effects auto. as soon as i sell it i will work on the car that i have in my signature below.. i am already paying for it, but it will be awsome.. thanks again for all help. this forum rocks... <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://209.125.196.179/fiero/adams/FieroTig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
